course: dictionary
lesson: 6966
title: Words that show where something comes from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where a person or thing comes from. Panamanian is one of them. It means coming from or belonging to Panama, a country in Central America that joins North and South America. A Panamanian is a person from Panama.
explain: The clue is in the word itself. You can see Panama inside Panamanian, so the word is linked to that place. «The Panamanian golden frog now survives only in breeding centres.» Its name tells you it comes from Panama. Ask: what place is this word linked to? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Panama is famous for the Panama Canal, which lets ships pass between the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans. So you might read about Panamanian food, the Panamanian flag or a Panamanian city. In each phrase, Panamanian means something from Panama.
fact: Panamanian means coming from or belonging to Panama.
fact: A Panamanian is a person from Panama.
fact: Words like Panamanian, Italian and Canadian show where something comes from.
fact: Panama is a country in Central America that joins North and South America.
fact: The Panama Canal lets ships pass between the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans.
exercise: «The Panamanian golden frog now survives only in breeding centres.» What does Panamanian show about the frog? | Which river it swims in | How fast it hops | *Where it comes from, Panama | The colour of its skin
exercise: What is a Panamanian? | A person from Spain | *A person from Panama | A large city in Europe | A kind of frog
exercise: Which phrase means something from Panama? | Scottish porridge | Italian pizza | Canadian maple syrup | *Panamanian food
test: Panama is a country that joins which two parts of America? | Africa and Europe | Australia and Antarctica | East and West Asia | *North and South America
test: Which word tells you a thing belongs to Panama? | Panama Canal? no, Pacific | Caribbean | *Panamanian | Atlantic
exam: The Panama Canal lets ships pass between which two oceans? | Arctic and Atlantic | *Atlantic and Pacific | Pacific and Indian | Indian and Arctic
